/* Grape vocabularies for FP_RULES["Wine Detail"]. Grape(s) is free text and has to be,
   because a strict list cannot hold "Colombard, Chardonnay", so these match as
   substrings and a blend matches every variety it names.

   SAUVIGNON IS THE TRAP. A bare /sauvignon/ matches inside "Cabernet Sauvignon", which
   is how the first Cabernet in the file came out scored as an aromatic terpene white:
   measured on santa-helena-varietal-cabernet-sauvignon-2025, aroma=aromatic c0.6. The
   alternative was written for Sauvignon Blanc. Anything here that could sit inside a
   longer variety name is therefore written out in full.

   Lookbehind would be the tidy fix and is deliberately NOT used. A regex literal the
   browser cannot parse throws at load and takes the whole script with it, which is the
   same class of hazard as the setScreenMode chain, and it would fail on the oldest
   Safari rather than on anything testable here.

   Non-ASCII is written as \u escapes rather than as literals, so no vocabulary can ever
   be the thing a mojibake scan trips over. */
const GRAPE_AROMATIC=/riesling|gew|muscat|moscato|viognier|torront|sauvignon\s+blanc|albari|malvasia|\bm(u|ü)ller|scheurebe|kerner/i;
const GRAPE_NEUTRAL=/colombard|ugni|trebbiano|chasselas|pinot\s+grigio|silvaner|macabeo|verdejo|chardonnay/i;
const GRAPE_FULL=/cabernet\s+sauvignon|syrah|shiraz|malbec|nebbiolo|tannat|petit\s+verdot|mourv|monastrell|touriga|aglianico|zinfandel|petite\s+sirah|carmen|sagrantino/i;
const GRAPE_LIGHT=/pinot\s+noir|gamay|cinsault|frappato|schiava|zweigelt|trousseau|poulsard|blaufr/i;
const GRAPE_CRISP=/riesling|sauvignon\s+blanc|chenin|albari|assyrtiko|verdicchio|gr(u|ü)ner|nebbiolo|barbera|sangiovese|gamay|pinot\s+noir|cortese|vermentino/i;
const GRAPE_SOFT=/viognier|grenache|garnacha|zinfandel|merlot|pinotage|marsanne|roussanne|s(e|é)millon/i;
const GRAPE_SAVOURY=/syrah|shiraz|nebbiolo|cabernet\s+franc|carmen|mourv|monastrell|tempranillo|sangiovese|pinotage|aglianico|xinomavro/i;

